{"_id":"68a7360d8ec3d8323af125c9","nodeId":"bQnOAu863hsHdyNMNyJop","roadmapSlug":"backend","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:53.149Z","description":"# N plus one problem\n\nThe N+1 problem occurs when an application retrieves a list then performs additional queries for each item's related data. Results in inefficient query multiplication (1 + N queries instead of optimized joins). Severely impacts performance with larger datasets. Solved through query optimization, joins, or batching techniques.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"In Detail Explanation of N+1 Problem","url":"https://medium.com/doctolib/understanding-and-fixing-n-1-query-30623109fe89","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4568"},{"type":"article","title":"What is the N+1 Problem","url":"https://planetscale.com/blog/what-is-n-1-query-problem-and-how-to-solve-it","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4569"},{"type":"video","title":"SQLite and the N+1 (no) problem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qPfAQY_RahA","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb456a"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T07:26:50.654Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d041699d","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"},{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d04169c7","title":"Scrimba - Backend Developer Career Path","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"http://scrimba.com/the-backend-developer-path-c0tbi0l98f?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/backend/content/bQnOAu863hsHdyNMNyJop.md"}
